WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you. Sit, sit.
Thank you.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.203 line:92%
Thank you. I appreciate it.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's great to be back
in my home of New York City.

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.574 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been on the road
a little bit.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.012 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was in Aruba.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:15.315
Whatever. It wasn't that great.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:18.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I'd call my mother.
I said, "I'm going to Aruba."

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:21.454 size:84% position:42% line:92%
She goes, "You flying?"

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:25.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, Mom.
The subway now goes to Aruba.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's 457 stops,
but it's like $2.75, so...

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:34.667
Yeah, the guy who books the room
is a guy named Aruba Ray.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.468 line:92%
That's the guy who books --

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:38.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, and he's almost
as bad as my mother, you know?

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, Aruba Ray goes,
"Come to Aruba."

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.043 line:92%
I said, "I don't want to fly."

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.178 line:92%
He goes, "Lenny, come to Aruba.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.113 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Do you like fresh fish?"

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:53.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was his sales pitch
for Aruba.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.888 size:88% position:44% line:92%
No, I like unfresh fish.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
I like a salmon that's
washed up on shore with, like,

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:00.727
one eye missing and a cigarette
coming out of his mouth.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, sauté that up.
I'm coming to Aruba, idiot.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
He did it again.
He did it again.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.469 line:92%
I think he has a thing for fish.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, more than
the Cousteau guy, you know?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm telling you.
He has a thing for fish.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
We go down there.
He takes me to dinner.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:18.845 size:88% position:44% line:92%
We're at the restaurant.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
He calls the waitress over
with the menu.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:24.084
He goes, "Excuse me. What's
the story with the salmon?"

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Who asks like that?

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What's the story
with the salmon?"

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:31.558 size:81% position:41%
"Uh, once upon a time,
there was a salmon...

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:35.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was gonna go to med school
but got caught in a net.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:38.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now he's being eaten
by an idiot."

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.836 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What's the story
with the salmon?"

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:50.443
It was the best of salmon,
it was the worst of salmon.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
People love food
more than I love food.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.482 size:75% position:38%
That I can tell you.
My wife loves food.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:56.449 line:92%
She takes me to restaurants.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know the big food thing
right now?

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.285 line:92%
You ever hear of farm-to-table?

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:03.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, this is
the biggest crock ever.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.624 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It really is.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
My wife dragged me to
a farm-to-table restaurant.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:11.631
The waiter, whispering,
sashays up to the table like...

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Hi.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you guys
dined with us before?"

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:20.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "No, but I've lived
on the planet before.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.543
Is this -- I pick from the list
and you bring it?

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.245 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.147 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I've done that."
It got worse.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.524 line:92%
Then he says, "Before we begin,

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:42.028
is anybody allergic to anything
I should be aware of?"

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.397 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I said, "Cats.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:47.767 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.537 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I'm not eating cats."

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:53.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now he hates me,
and I hate him. You know?

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they he goes,
"Let me tell you

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.610 size:81% position:41%
about the experience
you're about to have."

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:02.315 size:84% position:42%
And I look at my wife,
and she's going, "Ooh!"

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.017 line:92%
And I'm like, "Oh, my God.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:07.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is going to cost me
a small fortune."

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "This is a
farm-to-table restaurant.

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
We get all the food directly
from the farm

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we bring it
right to the table."

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm thinking,
"Where was all the other food

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
in all the other restaurants
to this point in my life

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.066 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
coming from?

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:24.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it coming
outer-space-to-table?

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:27.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just told my wife
anything she wanted to hear.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.741 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Placated her.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.977 size:81% position:41%
She goes, "What's with
this zucchini dish?"

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:33.213 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He goes, "Great choice."

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:36.783 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I'm like, "You suck."

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.884 line:92%
He just told her stories.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
"There's no sprays
on the zucchini.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.287 line:92%
There's no GMO's on the farm.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:45.458 size:81% position:41%
A small Venezuelan boy
raised it from a seed.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
He read it nursery rhymes
every day

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
until it grew to fruition
for you today.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:52.031
And he picked it just for you,
and he put it on his bicycle,

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:55.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he rode it the 200 miles
down from the farm.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.338 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Cha-ching, cha-ching!

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:03.109 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:08.381
And then he gave it to the chef,
who cried when he saw it.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:11.451 line:92%
He didn't want to cut it.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:14.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And that's $32."

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.389 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.523 line:92%
Farm-to-table. What a crock.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:21.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
It should be called
money-to-toilet.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:23.496 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.999 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.968
He goes, "What are you having?"
I said, "I'll have the fish."

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "Let me tell you
about the fish."

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.038 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"I don't want to know!"

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:34.007
'Cause I knew it was going to be
some dumb story like,

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:37.543
"We don't actually kill
the fish here. That's inhumane.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:38.478 size:75% position:38% line:92%
We just take a grill

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:41.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
and put it next to the pond,
and we just wait.

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:44.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
And eventually one
of the salmon is like,

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
'You know what?
I can't take it anymore.'

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:49.622 line:92%
And throws itself on the grill."

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.094 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:56.529 --> 00:05:02.368
"You're having the sayonara
salmon, which is $52.50."

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was livid.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he sashays
back up at the end.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:08.374
"Hi, again. Were you guys
thinking about dessert?"

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:11.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "I was thinking
about gun control."

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.846 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.382 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.488 size:88% position:44%
He goes, "Are you sure
you don't want dessert?"

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm this close to saying,
"Let me tell you

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:28.661 size:78% position:39%
about the experience
you're about to have.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:31.464 line:92%
It's called fist-to-face.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.566 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it's free!"

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.873 size:81% position:41%
Yeah, people love food
more than I love food.

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:41.808 line:92%
I get it. I get it, foodies.

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:44.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look. I'll give you a choice
of one of two things.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:47.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which would you take --
sex or soup?

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.748 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Okay, here's my theory.

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:52.652
If you're 32 years old or under,
you chose sex.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:55.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're over 50,
you chose soup.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.725
And everybody else in the middle
thought to themselves,

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.827 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"What kind of soup?"

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:02.929 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.664 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Thank you very much.

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:07.166 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.435 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:13.439 line:92%
-Lenny Marcus! Lenny Marcus!

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:19.612
His comedy album "Home and Away"
is available now on iTunes.

